            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Salsera713"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow! This was great! I'd never made haroset before because my mother was always in charge of all the Passover cooking. I was really impressed by this recipe as it tasted just like my mother's and it was easy to make. I doubled the amount of wine to make it more moist and it was delicious!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "romans8_38-39"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this recipe for our Messianic Passover Seder this weekend. It was a hit! I chopped the apples up into 1/4\" pieces and ran the nuts through my Magic Bullet to make it more like mortar. (I also reduced the nuts by a half.)",
            "datePublished": "2015-04-05T14:43:31.887Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JamieSSW"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Maybe it's just me, but I prefer a slightly higher apples-to-nuts ratio. I also recommend increasing the wine, and consider substituting honey, or better yet, date syrup (the original flowing \"honey\"), for the sugar.",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-23T10:10:47.660Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cookie734"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is very similar to the recipe my mom used. I don't feel like the extra sugar is necessary (unless you're using a wine that's not that sweet). I used Manischewitz Blackberry, and it was sweet enough. I don't cut my apples too finely, and I like my walnuts chopped a little bit larger as well.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-27T14:28:00.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The recipe lacked a very important ingredient: Dates! No Haroset can be fantastic without it, only meiocre. My take: double the wine and add finely chopped dates. YUM!",
            "datePublished": "2003-04-13T13:53:50.437Z"
          },
